-- =====================
-- Schema Template: Replace {{KEYSPACE}} with regional keyspace (nam, eur, ocn, eas, sam, sas, gdpr)
-- Applied by ScyllaMigrationService at startup, phase 1 of 3 of the users.primary_front
-- int -> smallint narrowing.
--
-- Full sequence:
--   1. 006 (this file) adds users.primary_front_new (smallint, defaults to null).
--   2. ScyllaMigrationService.BackfillPrimaryFrontIntToNewAsync copies every non-null
--      users.primary_front (int) value into users.primary_front_new, ledger-guarded
--      per keyspace with scope 'primary_front_backfill_int_to_new:{keyspace}'.
--   3. 007 drops users.primary_front (int) and re-adds it as smallint.
--   4. ScyllaMigrationService.BackfillPrimaryFrontNewToPrimaryAsync copies the smallint
--      values back from users.primary_front_new into the re-added users.primary_front.
--   5. 008 drops users.primary_front_new.
--
-- Two backfills are required because Cassandra/Scylla can't RENAME a non-PK column and
-- can't ALTER COLUMN TYPE either; the only safe way to change primary_front from int to
-- smallint while preserving the column name is via a temp column round-trip.
--
-- Idempotence is handled by the ledger: a matching checksum in global.schema_migrations
-- skips re-application. If a boot crashes between the ALTER landing and the ledger row
-- being written, ExecuteStatements catches the "column already exists" InvalidQueryException
-- on re-run.
-- =====================

ALTER TABLE {{KEYSPACE}}.users ADD primary_front_new smallint;
